WEBVTT

00:12:57.333 --> 00:13:00.643
I prove myself to someone
from whom I want your approval.

00:13:00.667 --> 00:13:02.684
And that means that you have power.

00:13:02.708 --> 00:13:03.976
AG: Right.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.434
EP: It's not bad, it just is.

00:13:05.458 --> 00:13:09.601
So I think that's the thing
that I am still testing at this moment is,

00:13:09.625 --> 00:13:12.101
are we going to have
debate or conversation?

00:13:12.125 --> 00:13:13.601
Are we building on each other?

00:13:13.625 --> 00:13:15.851
AG: I don't know,
which do you think is better?

00:13:15.875 --> 00:13:17.184
(Laughter)

00:13:17.208 --> 00:13:19.309
EP: Which do you think is better, people?

00:13:19.333 --> 00:13:20.601
Help me.

00:13:20.625 --> 00:13:22.059
AG: I'm trying to empower you

00:13:22.083 --> 00:13:24.809
to shape the conversation
in the direction you want to go.

00:13:24.833 --> 00:13:28.351
No, I think that part of the reason
that I sometimes default to debate is,

00:13:28.375 --> 00:13:30.976
I think we sometimes learn new things